          "fields": {
            "display_title": "The paper presents a method for two-stage self-supervised RL, where an agent first acquires semantic concepts and second grounds language tokens to these concepts (object relationships, primarily). While motivated by language grounding, the training and evaluation paradigms do not include any natural language input from human users, and object relationships are limited to two binary predicates between three objects.",
